      "body": "## Overview\r\nEnable batch invariance (`VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT=1`) for `EleutherAI/pythia-70m` model unit test on XPU when `use_prompt_embeds=True` to avoid batch variance. Otherwise, this case fails because of mismatches between outputs generated from token IDs and prompt embeddings.\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n- In the model ut of pythia-70m on XPU, batch variance causes mismatched logprobs between prompts-based and embeddings-based generation, making this ut fail.\r\n- The root cause is that batch variance leads to different batch shapes. Then numerical differences occur on layer1 attn and accumulate across layers to the final output diff.\r\n- Turning on batch invariance can fix the issue and make this case pass on XPU.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\nTo reproduce:\r\n```\r\npytest -s -v tests/models/language/generation/test_common.py::test_models[True-False-5-32-EleutherAI/pythia-70m]\r\n```\r\n\r\nresult before this PR:\r\n```\r\nE                   AssertionError: Test0:\r\nE                   Matched tokens:     [187, 510, 418, 3338, 310, 247, 6422, 13, 3809, 13, 285, 3809, 14, 936, 14]\r\nE                   vllm:       '\\nThe LMS is a powerful, fast, and fast-to-be-based, and is a powerful, fast, and fast-to-be'  {1257: Logprob(logprob=-3.6824374198913574, rank=1, decoded_token='be'), 20704: Logprob(logprob=-3.6824374198913574, rank=2, decoded_token='memory'), 30238: Logprob(logprob=-3.6824374198913574, rank=3, decoded_token='measure'), 14983: Logprob(logprob=-3.6824374198913574, rank=4, decoded_token='anal'), 24212: Logprob(logprob=-3.6824374198913574, rank=5, decoded_token='kill')}\r\nE                   vllm_from_embeds:   '\\nThe LMS is a powerful, fast, and fast-to-the-fly (LMS) that is a powerful, fast, and fast-'  {783: Logprob(logprob=-3.7288930416107178, rank=1, decoded_token='the'), 1257: Logprob(logprob=-3.7288930416107178, rank=2, decoded_token='be'), 20704: Logprob(logprob=-3.7288930416107178, rank=3, decoded_token='memory'), 30238: Logprob(logprob=-3.7288930416107178, rank=4, decoded_token='measure'), 14983: Logprob(logprob=-3.7288930416107178, rank=5, decoded_token='anal')}\r\n\r\ntests/models/utils.py:244: AssertionError\r\n```\r\n\r\nresult after this PR: `PASSED`.\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n### Root cause: batch variance introduces numerical differences amplified across layers\r\nLocal tracing showed different batching for the same prompts:\r\n```\r\nToken-ID inputs:   (step 0) prefill [20, 21]\r\nEmbedding inputs:  (step 0) prefill [21] → (step 1) [decode 1, prefill 20]\r\n```\r\nDifferent batch shapes introduce numerical differences in attn that propagate through the model and change the generated outputs. For the first prompt, the differences in attention tensors between token-id-based and embedding-based generation are shown below (diff = `max|a − b|`):\r\n\r\nLayer | Q diff | K diff | V diff | Attn output diff\r\n-- | -- | -- | -- | --\r\n0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0\r\n1 | 9.77e-4 | 1.95e-3 | 9.77e-4 | 4.88e-4\r\n2 | 3.91e-3 | 3.13e-2 | 1.95e-3 | 1.95e-3\r\n3 | 0.125 | 3.13e-2 | 1.95e-3 | 2.93e-3\r\n4 | 0.375 | 3.13e-2 | 1.95e-3 | 0.136\r\n5 | 2.5 | 0.133 | 3.49e-2 | 0.878\r\n\r\n### Another solution \r\n**Following ROCm to change `max_num_seqs` from 2 to 1 can also remove the effects of batch variance and make this ut pass on XPU.** This is clean but probably a workaround. As stated in the comments below, this was configured because batch invariance was not supported at that time. https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/ed1a7307950ab5e6593d25123579ed7ca998b350/tests/models/language/generation/test_common.py#L202-L205\r\nNow batch invariance has been basically supported (pls see https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/27433) and my local test shows it works on this ut. So this PR enables batch invariance for this case on XPU to fix its failure.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\r\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\r\n\r\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\r\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\r\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\r\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\r\n</details>",
